From c4b215d7c66e8b483ec14dbff820408bf865ec66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:51:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] LoneTeamVsCpu: a lone 2-human Teamplay entry gets its own
 room after the fill timer

After FillAfter (rolling, capped by MaxFillWait) a 2-human team with no compatible
opponent gets a room by itself: CheckMatching lists just its two clients in group 0,
so the game fills the other side with CPUs. Config OnlineMatching.LoneTeamVsCpu
(default false). Log line: MATCH room=N <world> lone-team-vs-cpu T[a,b] vs CPU.
1 new test (130 total pass).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Server-Infinite/Matchmaking/Matchmaker.cs     | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../Config/OnlineMatchingConfigurations.cs    |  4 +++
 Server-Infinite/Program.cs                    |  1 +
 Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/HangFixTests.cs       | 27 +++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 61 insertions(+)

